    {
     "user": "Design a low-carbon grout paste: mini-slump flow diameter >= 200 mm and 7-day compressive strength >= 30 MPa, minimise CO2. Space: w/b 0.30-0.50, OPC required, class F fly ash 0-0.5. Run without asking.",
     "text": "I’ll run the inverse design over the requested ranges, with OPC required and Class F fly ash capped at 0.5, and prioritize the lowest modeled CO₂ among mixes meeting both targets.\n**No candidate met both constraints.** The inverse-design search screened 8,192 mixes and returned three candidates, but each had a median mini-slump flow below 200 mm. Since flow is a weak model, treat its estimate as order-of-magnitude guidance; the 80% interval for each candidate was wide.\n\nThe lowest-CO₂ candidate returned was **50% OPC / 50% Class F fly ash, w/b 0.388**. Its estimates were:\n\n- Mini-slump flow: **179.1 [90.6, 292.3] mm**; estimated chance of meeting 200 mm: **0.41**\n- 7-day compressive strength: **26.0 [16.6, 56.7] MPa**; estimated chance of meeting 30 MPa: **0.43**\n- CO₂: **0.433 kg/kg powder** and **555.3 kg/m³**\n\nThis is a low-carbon lead for further trials, not a qualifying design. The solver’s reported joint feasibility was **0.176**; it assumes the target probabilities are independent. A published exact-tier analogue, M1, used OPC/Class F fly ash at **85/15**, w/b **0.30**, and PCE **0.50%** (DOI: [10.3389/fmats.2021.712551](https://doi.org/10.3389/fmats.2021.712551)); it is a reference mix, not evidence that the requested thresholds are met.\n\nDefaults used: paste system; 7-day strength; comp_cube50 specimens; moist curing; no aggregate. The tool did not state an admixture dosage for the candidates, so none is reported here. Experimental verification is needed, especially for flow.\n\nGenerated files: `result.json`, `report.md`, `candidates.csv`, `literature.csv`, `pareto.png`, and `parallel_coords.png` in `C:\\Users\\User\\3D Printing Concrete Prediction\\artifacts\\reports\\agent\\20261017-013804-3ed5\\design_Low-carbon grout paste`.\n",
